    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40599" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rē^-clīvis</span></b> , e
		(also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-vus</span></b> , a, um),
			adj.
		clivus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>leaning backwards</i>, <i>sloping</i>, <i>inclined</i> (late Lat.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">campo ad solem reclivi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Pall. 1, 6, 15</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tabulae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 7, 2, 3</span></i>
			 (al. reclines).—Form reclivus: nave
			reclivā, Ven. Fort. <i><span class="en">Mart. 3</span></i>.</div>
